  "label": "Generalization Aware Binding Model Benchmarking",
  "related": [
    "model-rna-906f",
    "builder-capsid-20a5",
    "cryo-structure-34d6"
  ],
  "secondary_categories": [
    "structural"
  ],
  "slug": "optimal-transport-flow-matching-ea35",
  "summary": "Cross-state, disordered-partner and cofolding benchmarks, alongside encoder profiling, indicate reported binding accuracy tracks evaluation design as much as model class.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is that evaluation construction is being treated as a first-class modeling decision in structure- and sequence-based interaction prediction. The OneProt profiling study finds dataset properties, not encoder architecture or modality mix, dominate separability for allosteric versus orthosteric site classification. AllositeUltra introduces AsBench2, a cross-state benchmark forcing prediction on both apo and substrate-bound structures rather than a single conformer. The cofolding benchmark of AlphaFold3, RoseTTAFold3, Boltz-2 and Chai-1 on kinase and GPCR complexes shows correct ligand placement is decoupled from accurate protein conformation, so aggregate success metrics conflate distinct failure modes. FlexENN adds an evaluation set spanning folded and intrinsically disordered partner complexes; the M2OR work tests cross-dataset transfer to iOBPdb; the RNA-small molecule survey treats evaluation protocol alongside methodology. Architecturally diverse entries (Bonbon, RSMBind, DTBNet, MBFGNK) are differentiated mainly by the held-out regimes on which they are claimed to hold up.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-12"
}
